                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ni no Kuni II: Revenant Kingdom – A beautifully wholesome RPG full of heart and charm!\n\nNi no Kuni II is an absolutely beautiful and wonderfully wholesome RPG. This is how you create a compelling, memorable adventure without having to make everything dark, miserable, or unnecessarily edgy.\n\nThe world is bursting with charm, the characters are genuinely lovable, and the story knows exactly when to make you laugh and when to break your heart. It's the kind of adventure that sticks with you long after the credits roll.\n\nAnd I still can't think about that damn booger without laughing.\n\nThe combat is perfectly enjoyable, even if it isn't anything revolutionary. Surprisingly, even the overworld RTS-style battles manage to be entertaining without overstaying their welcome. They're a nice change of pace rather than another tedious mechanic you wish you could skip.\n\nWhat I appreciate most is the game's willingness to be lighthearted and playful. There's so much personality in its world, and it never feels ashamed of being a colourful, whimsical fantasy adventure. It still manages to tell a meaningful story with emotional weight, without constantly drowning itself in doom and gloom.\n\nI genuinely wish we had more RPGs like this. Games that aren't afraid to be charming, funny, heartfelt, and just a little bit silly while still delivering a proper adventure.\n\nA beautifully crafted RPG that proves you don't need endless misery to tell a memorable story. Sometimes a little magic, a lot of heart, and a good laugh are more than enough.\n\nAnd of course...\n\n\"YOU OWE ME!\"",
